 "prompt": "The repository at /testbed has a bug, described below. Fix it by changing the source code; do not modify or\nadd tests. When you are done, the project's existing test suite should pass.\n\n<issue>\n# Multi-line comments are not being parsed correctly\n\nI found an issue with the comment parsing in the tokenizer. When using multi-line comments, the comment text is not being extracted correctly.\n\n## Reproduction\n\nHere's a simple example that demonstrates the issue:\n\n```python\nfrom sqlglot import parse_one\n\n# This works fine\nsql_with_single_line = \"SELECT 1 -- This is a comment\"\nparsed = parse_one(sql_with_single_line)\nprint(parsed)  # Works as expected\n\n# This fails\nsql_with_multi_line = \"\"\"\nSELECT 1\n/* This is a \n   multi-line comment */\nFROM dual\n\"\"\"\nparsed = parse_one(sql_with_multi_line)\nprint(parsed)  # The comment text is incorrect\n```\n\nWhen examining the parsed result, you'll notice that the multi-line comment text is truncated or contains incorrect characters. The issue appears to be in the comment extraction logic in the tokenizer.\n\nI noticed this happens specifically with the `/* */` style comments, where the comment text is not being sliced correctly. The single-line comments with `--` seem to work fine.\n</issue>\n",
